{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Engine comparison, THIRD run (antifungal-amenable-mite), recorded 2026-11-12 12:03 PST. It supersedes both earlier comparison comments.\n\nWhy: LLM-Review on Gerrit 3366 PS3 found that both engines reviewed in one shared disposable store, so the agent's file tools could read the pipeline's Pass-1 checkpoint files under .rebar/cache. Verified: a pipeline review leaves 10 such files in the store. Each engine now reviews in its own identically seeded store.\n\nThis run used the Anthropic API path (REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE=.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml; frontier = claude-opus-5-5, standard = claude-sonnet-5-5) because Bedrock is under the daily spend-cap deny. Same corpus (digest c386161d43b1…), all 11 rows.\n\nResults (src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json, valid=true, no errors, floor blocks or INDETERMINATEs):\n- Verdict agreement: 9/11 (0.82). Confusion matrix (pipeline rows × agentic columns): PASS→PASS 8, PASS→BLOCK 1, BLOCK→BLOCK 1, BLOCK→PASS 1.\n- Blocking flips: 2.\n- Finding overlap (token-set Jaccard ≥ 0.5, DET excluded): 1 matched, 127 pipeline-only, 53 agentic-only. This is a lexical lower bound.\n- Agreement with the historical pipeline verdict: 5/10 for each engine.\n\nThe 3 runs gave 8/11, 10/11 and 9/11 agreement on the same 11 plans. Run-to-run variance of ±1 plan is the same size as the engine difference, so 11 plans cannot separate the engines."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794514062284381718,"uuid":"8d0e7a2f-566b-4606-8011-208dc914a6d6"}